1
00:00:14,060 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,880
kicking a little pebble,
I leap off with a bear,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to Kashiwa, the type who was out jogging,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,800
they laughed at me for staying
just as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:37,440
Even if I somehow stir up some energy,

6
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:38,700
gutsy, there's something saved up.

7
00:00:38,700 --> 00:00:41,040
not a single nightmare changes.

8
00:00:41,040 --> 00:00:43,880
The streetscape is kinder now, you know.

9
00:00:44,660 --> 00:00:47,020
Because the crows are cawing,

10
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,720
the sun has already gone down.

11
00:00:49,600 --> 00:00:53,860
Can you really see the yakitori stall?

12
00:00:54,880 --> 00:00:57,500
Of the pointed hat...

13
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:04,060
from the people to Daishaku-den,
the sunset falls.

14
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,080
Tomorrow too,
it ends with a drop, doesn't it.

15
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:12,800
Is it a magazine? Happiness again, they say.

16
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:16,300
Because I'm the fool who
only realized after losing it.

17
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,860
Desert Island Golf

18
00:01:30,320 --> 00:01:32,360
The golf competition for
next week has been decided.

19
00:01:32,740 --> 00:01:33,760
That's good to hear.

20
00:01:34,500 --> 00:01:36,000
We've been busy lately.

21
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,420
Golf in nature is nice, you know.

22
00:01:38,420 --> 00:01:39,300
Yeah, that's right.

23
00:01:40,320 --> 00:01:43,040
Nature can be a relaxation too, can't it?

24
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:47,260
You lot, golf has nothing
to do with nature, you know.

25
00:01:47,260 --> 00:01:48,660
Why is that?

26
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,480
Cutting down the forest that
was there from the start,

27
00:01:53,480 --> 00:01:55,320
Covering the whole course with grass,

28
00:01:55,320 --> 00:01:58,500
they build artificial ponds and
bunkers to make it harder to hit.

29
00:01:59,480 --> 00:02:01,900
Where's the nature in
a golf course like that?

30
00:02:02,440 --> 00:02:03,980
That's true, but

31
00:02:03,980 --> 00:02:05,700
Where's the relaxation in that?

32
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,160
You're right.

33
00:02:08,620 --> 00:02:09,720
Who are you?

34
00:02:10,100 --> 00:02:12,600
I'm the golf entertainment
section chief at our company.

35
00:02:13,060 --> 00:02:14,460
Nice to meet you all.

36
00:02:15,260 --> 00:02:16,820
Just as Lord Ryochi says,

37
00:02:16,820 --> 00:02:20,140
today's golf can be said to
have nothing to do with nature.

38
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:23,500
Originally, golf was something
shepherds played to pass the time.

39
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:25,901
hitting stones,

40
00:02:25,951 --> 00:02:29,360
it's said to have begun as a game
of knocking them into rabbit burrows.

41
00:02:30,480 --> 00:02:32,764
Now, not only golf courses,

42
00:02:32,814 --> 00:02:35,440
but golf clubs are made of aluminum,
titanium, and so on,

43
00:02:35,760 --> 00:02:39,200
and some are high-tech models
costing hundreds of thousands of yen.

44
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:43,600
With all that, it's no wonder people
say it's the opposite of nature.

45
00:02:43,860 --> 00:02:45,520
We see eye to eye, Otaku.

46
00:02:46,420 --> 00:02:49,440
No, I've thought the same for a while now.

47
00:02:49,980 --> 00:02:53,960
What do you think, Keichi-sama? For this competition,
let's go back to basics

48
00:02:55,320 --> 00:02:56,540
and play golf

49
00:02:56,980 --> 00:02:59,400
Yeah, that's great! Let's do it!

50
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:01,800
Well, then, I'll leave it to you.

51
00:03:02,320 --> 00:03:02,720
Thank you very much.

52
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,500
Then I'll help plan the competition too.

53
00:03:06,920 --> 00:03:09,400
Entertainment section chief,
let's sit down and talk over here.

54
00:03:09,860 --> 00:03:11,740
No, golf in general is, well, you know...

55
00:03:14,160 --> 00:03:15,660
Senpai has been like this since long ago,

56
00:03:15,660 --> 00:03:18,540
he always said golf was a rich man's hobby,

57
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:22,580
and he's so jealous of the rich, that guy.

58
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:24,120
This competition is scary.

59
00:03:32,440 --> 00:03:35,140
By the way, which island are we heading to?

60
00:03:35,140 --> 00:03:38,920
It's the oldest island, in the middle of the South Pacific,
an absolutely outrageous remote island.

61
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:41,480
You'll be amazed, it's an island, really.

62
00:03:41,480 --> 00:03:43,800
Amazing, really, an island.

63
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:45,960
I've never heard of it.

64
00:03:46,380 --> 00:03:47,780
That's understandable.

65
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:52,800
Since it's an island no human has
ever set foot on in recorded history,

66
00:03:52,800 --> 00:03:55,460
Can you even play golf in a place like that?

67
00:03:55,940 --> 00:04:00,000
That's what I told you! This time we're
playing golf in the middle of nature.

68
00:04:02,760 --> 00:04:04,420
We're almost there!

69
00:04:19,320 --> 00:04:20,660
Welcome, all good?

70
00:04:21,180 --> 00:04:22,400
Thank you for having us.

71
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:23,560
All good, all good.

72
00:04:24,120 --> 00:04:26,740
Ryo-tsu, what happened to your golf bag?

73
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:30,000
You didn't bring one in the first place,
did you?

74
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:33,380
You can't hit without clubs, you know.

75
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:35,720
The clubs are all prepared properly.

76
00:04:35,720 --> 00:04:37,840
Let's head to the hole quickly.

77
00:04:43,900 --> 00:04:45,920
W-well, it's truly the great outdoors!

78
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:48,840
Speaking of which,
you've got a lot of personality, don't you?

79
00:04:52,920 --> 00:04:55,540
This is this time's golf club.

80
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,040
This one?

81
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,140
Isn't this an akaza staff?

82
00:05:00,140 --> 00:05:02,020
It's a natural material.

83
00:05:02,020 --> 00:05:03,260
What's akaza?

84
00:05:03,960 --> 00:05:07,000
It's an annual plant from
China with sturdy stems.

85
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,840
It's a staff that a thousand people carry.

86
00:05:09,800 --> 00:05:11,420
That staff.

87
00:05:11,420 --> 00:05:14,380
If you use the root as the head,
it can be used as a club.

88
00:05:16,200 --> 00:05:16,560
And then...

89
00:05:19,540 --> 00:05:21,560
We'll use potatoes for the balls.

90
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:22,620
Potatoes.

91
00:05:23,800 --> 00:05:27,200
Lost balls normally stay as
they are even after decades,

92
00:05:27,200 --> 00:05:30,980
but potatoes sprout roots there
and eventually turn back into nature.

93
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:34,360
That's definitely 100% natural material.

94
00:05:34,860 --> 00:05:37,880
In that case, rounder ones would be better.

95
00:05:38,800 --> 00:05:41,780
But hitting everything with
just this one club is tough.

96
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:45,500
This side is pretty bumpy too.

97
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,720
Alright, shall we get started?

98
00:05:53,340 --> 00:05:57,680
Before that, I'll announce the
winner's prize for this competition.

99
00:05:58,260 --> 00:05:59,160
The winner will receive

100
00:05:59,780 --> 00:06:00,500
this.

101
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:06,300
a pair of tickets for a luxury cruise around the world,
provided by the Nakagawa Group.

102
00:06:07,360 --> 00:06:10,380
Now I'm really fired up!

103
00:06:11,040 --> 00:06:13,280
It'd be great to go with Jodie.

104
00:06:14,420 --> 00:06:17,840
I'd love to go with Nana-chan too.

105
00:06:23,320 --> 00:06:25,920
Can the winning prize be
turned into cash, right?

106
00:06:25,920 --> 00:06:28,360
Of course, that's fine too.

107
00:06:28,960 --> 00:06:32,060
A round-the-world trip won't
cost less than ten million yen.

108
00:06:34,480 --> 00:06:36,780
All right, let's get started right away.

109
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:42,220
The first hole is this way.

110
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:45,740
Beyond this jungle is the beach.

111
00:06:46,580 --> 00:06:48,380
There's a meerkat hole here.

112
00:06:48,960 --> 00:06:51,180
That serves as the cup for the first hole.

113
00:06:51,800 --> 00:06:53,700
So the holes are natural too

114
00:06:54,120 --> 00:06:56,040
It's a par-5 long hole.

115
00:06:56,880 --> 00:06:58,980
Then please decide the order of play.

116
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,800
I'm the owner, right?

117
00:07:10,620 --> 00:07:12,000
This is awkward to hit from.

118
00:07:13,280 --> 00:07:15,160
Hurry up, Nakagawa.

119
00:07:15,660 --> 00:07:16,100
Yes.

120
00:07:24,220 --> 00:07:25,300
It curved.

121
00:07:27,180 --> 00:07:29,900
Reiko-san, potatoes curve a lot.

122
00:07:30,440 --> 00:07:31,300
I'll be careful.

123
00:07:38,080 --> 00:07:39,720
This time, to the left.

124
00:07:44,540 --> 00:07:45,520
What?!

125
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:48,500
Senpai, potatoes won't work.

126
00:07:49,080 --> 00:07:52,060
That's not true! Look closely at the potato!

127
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:55,220
You just have to calculate
these irregular dimples.

128
00:07:55,220 --> 00:07:57,580
If you spin it, it flies straight.

129
00:07:57,580 --> 00:07:59,780
We use the wind to add distance.

130
00:08:00,640 --> 00:08:03,880
And this part of the club is the sweet spot.

131
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:05,540
This angle is good.

132
00:08:05,980 --> 00:08:09,020
If you hit at this angle,
at the moment of impact,

133
00:08:09,020 --> 00:08:11,860
it spins hard to the right
and flies in a straight line.

134
00:08:13,280 --> 00:08:14,080
It's only going to hit the ceiling.

135
00:08:14,080 --> 00:08:15,280
No way, that's impossible.

136
00:08:16,240 --> 00:08:17,660
Well then, let's give it a try.

137
00:08:20,020 --> 00:08:24,520
In nature golf, the basics of golf
you've known until now don't work at all.

138
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:27,500
I'd say it'll go about 300 yards.

139
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:28,960
Alright.

140
00:08:32,040 --> 00:08:32,900
Whoosh

141
00:08:34,680 --> 00:08:36,180
It doesn't curve at all.

142
00:08:37,420 --> 00:08:38,500
Not bad.

143
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:41,000
With equipment like that...

144
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,840
Well then, shall we go?

145
00:08:44,040 --> 00:08:46,840
What should we do about
balls that land in the jungle?

146
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:49,740
Won't they all end up as lost balls?

147
00:08:51,480 --> 00:08:54,000
They will absolutely not become lost balls.

148
00:08:54,620 --> 00:08:58,380
After this,
these hounds will serve as your caddies.

149
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:01,100
Entertainment Section Chief,
what do you mean?

150
00:09:01,420 --> 00:09:04,900
Since the hounds have already been
made to sniff all of your scents,

151
00:09:04,900 --> 00:09:07,740
they'll rely on that to find the balls.

152
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:34,740


153
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,200
Somewhere like this,

154
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:54,040
there's no way we can
get it out of here, right?

155
00:09:57,540 --> 00:09:59,740
I'll move it just a little.

156
00:10:01,480 --> 00:10:02,820
Bite him!

157
00:10:02,820 --> 00:10:03,680
Bite him!

158
00:10:04,740 --> 00:10:05,660
You just cheated!

159
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:09,280
This dog's been trained
to bite anyone who cheats!

160
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:15,100
Sorry, I'll take the one-stroke penalty,
so please let me shoot from a distance.

161
00:10:17,420 --> 00:10:21,220
Just getting the potato out of
the jungle cost me ten shots!

162
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:24,640
Good boy, good boy!

163
00:10:30,840 --> 00:10:32,340
What a huge number of birds.

164
00:10:33,260 --> 00:10:36,280
This island is also known as Bird Island.

165
00:10:39,520 --> 00:10:42,340
There's a meerkat burrow up ahead.

166
00:10:45,800 --> 00:10:46,940
Whose is it?

167
00:10:48,660 --> 00:10:50,900
Looks like my potato, doesn't it?

168
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:52,280
Alright, go!

169
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:53,000
Yes.

170
00:10:59,040 --> 00:11:00,440
The birds are bothering me.

171
00:11:05,820 --> 00:11:06,840
Nice shot!

172
00:11:11,500 --> 00:11:12,620
Why again?

173
00:11:12,620 --> 00:11:14,800
It's a lost ball

174
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:15,620
No way.

175
00:11:18,020 --> 00:11:19,420
What kind of golf is this?

176
00:11:20,360 --> 00:11:21,920
I don't get it at all.

177
00:11:23,380 --> 00:11:25,180
Just be surprised, then.

178
00:11:25,180 --> 00:11:27,740
I'm definitely getting that ten million.

179
00:11:41,440 --> 00:11:43,100
Right, my turn next.

180
00:11:50,120 --> 00:11:51,480
Is that where I'm aiming?

181
00:11:51,480 --> 00:11:53,400
Aaaaaah!

182
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:04,600
Just as I planned.
Government is good at this kind of thing.

183
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:08,720
Just hurry up already, aaaaaah!

184
00:12:08,720 --> 00:12:09,480
Failed!

185
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,380
Ow

186
00:12:26,720 --> 00:12:28,040
What a huge number.

187
00:12:28,560 --> 00:12:30,020
That was terrifying, wasn't it?

188
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:32,660
Thanks to the birds being gone,

189
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:34,520
it's become a lot easier to shoot!

190
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:43,420
My ball is...

191
00:12:45,540 --> 00:12:46,700
Ah!

192
00:12:47,040 --> 00:12:49,360
My ball is being eaten!

193
00:12:49,980 --> 00:12:52,960
Its dimples have completely changed shape!

194
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,300
Damn it!

195
00:12:55,980 --> 00:12:56,680
Nice!

196
00:12:57,320 --> 00:12:57,760
Thank you.

197
00:12:59,500 --> 00:13:01,520
It has certainly gotten easier, hasn't it.

198
00:13:01,520 --> 00:13:03,480
I somehow managed to keep it to a bogey.

199
00:13:06,660 --> 00:13:09,480
Hmph! I'm going for an eagle!

200
00:13:18,380 --> 00:13:21,180
Damn!

201
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,960
Oh no! It's ruined! I got a par!

202
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:28,820
This is a par-3 short hole.

203
00:13:29,460 --> 00:13:31,495
Hold on a sec, timeout,

204
00:13:31,545 --> 00:13:35,020
I'm going to go light the way,
so Nakagawa, take your shot first.

205
00:13:35,720 --> 00:13:37,560
Honestly, Ryo-chan.

206
00:13:46,380 --> 00:13:47,660
K-Ken-chan!

207
00:13:48,020 --> 00:13:49,200
What was that just now?

208
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:55,380
This hole has small waves beneath it,

209
00:13:55,380 --> 00:13:59,860
a trap course where water
spurts up when the waves hit it.

210
00:14:00,600 --> 00:14:02,660
You should have told us that first!

211
00:14:08,440 --> 00:14:10,320
We can't take a shot like this!

212
00:14:10,320 --> 00:14:14,100
You two, use your heads a little.

213
00:14:15,060 --> 00:14:16,260
What do you mean by that?

214
00:14:20,160 --> 00:14:23,100
Just aim from where the waves don't reach.

215
00:14:25,900 --> 00:14:27,800
This is dynamic golf!

216
00:14:28,280 --> 00:14:28,680
And then?

217
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:35,640
Yay!

218
00:14:35,640 --> 00:14:37,100
It's a hole-in-one!

219
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,720
Senpai!

220
00:14:46,260 --> 00:14:47,420
Are you all right? Ryotsu!

221
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:50,860
Damn it! What the hell is this?!

222
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:53,300
This is really dynamic!

223
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:57,080
That's just nature taking its course,
so we can't complain

224
00:15:00,720 --> 00:15:02,260
S-senpai!

225
00:15:08,660 --> 00:15:10,620
Wow! It's an ichthyosaurus!

226
00:15:10,940 --> 00:15:12,420
This really is nature in all its glory!

227
00:15:13,960 --> 00:15:15,960
Is this the White Hare of Inaba or what?!

228
00:15:16,220 --> 00:15:17,780
Wh-what, hey!

229
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:25,360
What incredible vitality!

230
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:26,900
Truly...

231
00:15:26,900 --> 00:15:28,080
It's the suction-cup hole!

232
00:15:32,980 --> 00:15:34,620
Yes! It's a birdie!

233
00:15:36,220 --> 00:15:37,740
Good luck, you two!

234
00:15:37,860 --> 00:15:38,580
Damn it!

235
00:15:38,920 --> 00:15:41,920
You two have outstanding athletic ability,
after all.

236
00:15:43,420 --> 00:15:45,822
There's an even more amazing
course in the second half,

237
00:15:45,872 --> 00:15:47,780
and we'll pull away at the final hole!

238
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:51,420
Yeah, that place is...

239
00:15:58,480 --> 00:15:59,900
Nice kick!

240
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:05,740
If we use that rock,
we could even get a hole-in-one...

241
00:16:28,680 --> 00:16:30,740
Why is there a Tyrannosaurus here?

242
00:16:30,740 --> 00:16:34,380
It's an island untouched by
humans since the age of dinosaurs.

243
00:16:37,300 --> 00:16:38,060
Meat eater!

244
00:16:38,060 --> 00:16:41,120
Sir, what are you doing?

245
00:16:41,120 --> 00:16:42,720
The 10 million is mine!

246
00:16:42,720 --> 00:16:46,140
I'm not giving up just
because of a Tyrannosaurus!

247
00:16:55,180 --> 00:16:57,800
Yay, another hole-in-one!

248
00:17:00,080 --> 00:17:01,120
What?

249
00:17:01,780 --> 00:17:02,920
Hey!

250
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:05,120
And it was a hole-in-one, too!

251
00:17:05,120 --> 00:17:05,860
Damn you!

252
00:17:05,860 --> 00:17:06,900
You little...!

253
00:17:06,900 --> 00:17:07,460
Come out!

254
00:17:07,460 --> 00:17:08,380
Damn it!

255
00:17:09,540 --> 00:17:10,700
Yes!

256
00:17:10,700 --> 00:17:11,740
Over here?

257
00:17:11,740 --> 00:17:13,060
Take that!

258
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:17,760
This is just the wild nature of this place

259
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:23,620
Yay!

260
00:17:23,620 --> 00:17:24,640
Trax!

261
00:17:26,720 --> 00:17:28,300
This is the 17th hole.

262
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:44,860
Sorry, senpai, sorry.

263
00:17:45,440 --> 00:17:47,600
Out of bounds, so it's a re-shot

264
00:17:47,600 --> 00:17:48,680
Out of bounds?

265
00:17:49,680 --> 00:17:50,680
Eeeehhh!

266
00:17:53,920 --> 00:17:58,600
If I take the penalty stroke,
Nakagawa will catch up to me. No way!

267
00:17:59,720 --> 00:18:00,260
Haa!

268
00:18:01,800 --> 00:18:07,860
Ryo-chan, you can't do it, come back!
It's not like I'm scared or anything!

269
00:18:08,460 --> 00:18:10,380
It's not a penalty, I swung from below, ugh!

270
00:18:10,380 --> 00:18:11,320
Ngh!

271
00:18:25,100 --> 00:18:26,860
I won't hand the victory to anyone.

272
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:27,760
I'm going to take it.

273
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:28,940
Prize money.

274
00:18:28,940 --> 00:18:30,140
10 million.

275
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:41,040
W-wow!

276
00:18:41,040 --> 00:18:42,840
Whoa, it went out!

277
00:18:42,840 --> 00:18:44,980
Terrifying determination.

278
00:18:45,540 --> 00:18:46,880
When money's involved,

279
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,840
he's the type who'd turn a crab into a hunter,
after all.

280
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:05,460
Somehow we got through with a bogey.

281
00:19:08,200 --> 00:19:10,020
Next is the final hole.

282
00:19:10,780 --> 00:19:11,820
Here we go, then.

283
00:19:12,360 --> 00:19:16,640
The cup on the final hole is this processed
"Bikkuri shita naa mou-san."

284
00:19:16,640 --> 00:19:20,740
By the way,
this is a super long hole, par 80.

285
00:19:21,480 --> 00:19:24,560
Par 80? Don't be ridiculous.

286
00:19:25,060 --> 00:19:28,300
The cup is that huge, so isn't it easy?

287
00:19:28,300 --> 00:19:31,160
The hole is certainly big, though.

288
00:19:31,800 --> 00:19:33,160
It's fine, it's fine, it's fine.

289
00:19:34,060 --> 00:19:37,700
Apparently the fastest way is
to climb up the right-hand route.

290
00:19:38,160 --> 00:19:40,660
Looks like you're really going all in.

291
00:19:47,140 --> 00:19:49,400
Crossing the jungle really is impossible,
after all.

292
00:19:50,580 --> 00:19:53,740
No, we have to get through
this jungle no matter what.

293
00:19:59,900 --> 00:20:06,980
Damn it! We were so close!

294
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:12,880
It's tough in this jungle,
not being able to see ahead.

295
00:20:13,400 --> 00:20:16,240
Yeah. That's why we're carrying
a compass and moving forward.

296
00:20:22,120 --> 00:20:22,840
What is this!

297
00:20:23,140 --> 00:20:24,540
It's a mass migration of snakes!

298
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:27,580
It's fine, it's fine, it's fine!

299
00:20:28,160 --> 00:20:30,180
Apparently there are a lot
of them this time of year.

300
00:20:30,660 --> 00:20:33,758
But the local staff says
they aren't poisonous, so

301
00:20:33,808 --> 00:20:35,040
Don't worry, it's fine.

302
00:20:35,460 --> 00:20:38,020
I'll take the penalty and go around.

303
00:20:38,680 --> 00:20:39,200
Me too.

304
00:20:40,060 --> 00:20:43,720
Those idiots have no backbone.
This is the shortest route!

305
00:20:43,920 --> 00:20:44,900
I'm going!

306
00:20:45,300 --> 00:20:46,400
Hey, w-wait, senpai!

307
00:20:46,820 --> 00:20:48,460
Leave him be, that idiot.

308
00:20:48,940 --> 00:20:50,180
Hey, this one. Okay.

309
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:54,940
Okay, okay, okay.

310
00:20:55,540 --> 00:20:58,060
Get out of the way! I can't see the ball!

311
00:21:00,600 --> 00:21:01,800
Okay, now's our chance.

312
00:21:08,640 --> 00:21:11,100
Hey, quit waiting!
It's hard to shoot like that, you know!

313
00:21:12,420 --> 00:21:13,680
Ow ow ow

314
00:21:13,680 --> 00:21:14,800
Whoa, ow ow

315
00:21:15,900 --> 00:21:16,880
Damn it!

316
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:18,580
Ouch!

317
00:21:19,560 --> 00:21:20,960
I got bitten badly.

318
00:21:21,940 --> 00:21:23,440
Are you okay, Ryo-chan?

319
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:25,740
I'm feeling a bit dizzy.

320
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,980
And I've got a fever too.

321
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:30,000
I'm fine, I'm fine, I'm fine.

322
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:34,040
The local staff said they
might be venomous snakes,

323
00:21:34,460 --> 00:21:35,980
You idiot.

324
00:21:39,780 --> 00:21:44,920
Aaaah, it's game over. I give up!

325
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:51,820
Eeeeh, I'm not giving up,
but I've already hit a yakuman-level shot.

326
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:55,200
But finally,
the processed food is coming into view!

327
00:21:57,000 --> 00:22:02,200
I'm at 76 so far.
Sink this and it's an albatross, baby! Yeah!

328
00:22:03,200 --> 00:22:06,260
Eh, something's shaking!

329
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:18,140
Just like Daishizen Golf, this is an
excitement worthy of the final hole.

330
00:22:18,960 --> 00:22:22,180
Idiot, this is no time for that!
It's dangerous!

331
00:22:22,820 --> 00:22:24,460
Let's get to lower ground quickly!

332
00:22:28,540 --> 00:22:31,620
Run, run! This means we win!

333
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,040
Okay, here it comes!

334
00:22:35,840 --> 00:22:36,520
Go!

335
00:22:39,920 --> 00:22:41,780
Yay! It's in the cup!

336
00:23:03,420 --> 00:23:05,500
Senpai, do you think he'll be all right?

337
00:23:05,840 --> 00:23:09,200
Don't worry.
That guy is tougher than a cockroach.

338
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:21,480
He really did sink it,
right before the lava came out.

339
00:23:22,160 --> 00:23:23,880
But nobody saw it.

340
00:23:23,880 --> 00:23:27,800
Senpai, I'm sorry, but since there's no victory,
that's the end of it.

341
00:23:29,060 --> 00:23:30,760
Ten million yen, just like that!

342
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:38,260
And next month, we'll play some
unnatural golf at a course in Tokyo.

343
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:41,940
You don't need to go out of your way to add
"unnatural" like that.

344
00:24:01,100 --> 00:24:04,640
Sandals anytime, scandals anytime,
don't you care about any of it?

345
00:24:05,420 --> 00:24:08,460
Playing it cool, every day!

346
00:24:08,460 --> 00:24:14,020
I crumpled up boredom like a
reprimand and tossed it away.

347
00:24:15,100 --> 00:24:18,520
Bare instincts, raw instincts,
going wild and stupid

348
00:24:19,580 --> 00:24:22,320
Reckless and broke, so what's the harm?

349
00:24:22,320 --> 00:24:23,320
That's not it

350
00:24:24,120 --> 00:24:26,700
My way, doing whatever I want

351
00:24:26,700 --> 00:24:28,100
Just gonna do it

352
00:24:28,100 --> 00:24:28,860
Amazing

353
00:24:28,860 --> 00:24:30,900
The stubborn Chief's thunderbolt

354
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:32,680
Smoke from the head

355
00:24:33,500 --> 00:24:35,720
Run away and it's Kame-ana

356
00:24:35,720 --> 00:24:36,160
Kame-ana

357
00:24:36,160 --> 00:24:37,460
Well, that's wonderful, isn't it?

358
00:24:37,460 --> 00:24:38,280
Ohhh!

359
00:24:38,280 --> 00:24:39,900
In the flower of Edo,

360
00:24:39,900 --> 00:24:40,600
Jaizō!

361
00:24:40,600 --> 00:24:42,120
Ryōzan Daifun!

362
00:24:42,120 --> 00:24:42,980
Maido!

363
00:24:42,980 --> 00:24:45,460
Raging wild,

364
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:47,640
Workers' play, 9×2!

365
00:24:47,640 --> 00:24:49,040
Q game, Q game!

366
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:51,280
Here in the moisture, boldly, water!

367
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:56,460
Today's end, today's end, dark end,
a place to sleep, a place to live.

368
00:24:57,060 --> 00:25:00,340
Yabura coach, bura coach,
paiko paiko paiko no...

369
00:25:00,340 --> 00:25:03,140
Shūringan, Shūringan no Gūrindai,

370
00:25:03,140 --> 00:25:06,340
Gūrindai no Ponpokotei no Ponpokunā no...

371
00:25:06,340 --> 00:25:07,940
Super-investigator Chōsuke!

372
00:25:15,060 --> 00:25:17,160
A major incident happened
at the Honda house!

373
00:25:17,160 --> 00:25:19,540
My little sister Ibu is
apparently going off to Africa.

374
00:25:19,540 --> 00:25:20,800
Honda, pull yourself together!

375
00:25:22,320 --> 00:25:26,640
Well, it can't be helped. Stand between Dad
and Ibu and give him a real piece of your mind!

376
00:25:26,640 --> 00:25:31,860
It's hopeless after all, isn't it? Next time,
again and again. Honda family, see you then!

